      "title": "Vertex on the Move",
      "type": "scene",
    },
    {
      "category": "Assessment",
      "content": "A parabola has vertex (3, -4) and opens upward. Which equation shows this most directly?",
      "correctOption": 1,
      "explanation": "Vertex form is y = a(x - h)² + k with vertex (h, k) = (3, -4), and a > 0 for upward — giving y = (x - 3)² - 4.",
      "id": "final-check",
      "quizOptions": [
        "y = (x + 3)² - 4",
        "y = (x - 3)² - 4",
        "y = (x - 3)² + 4",
        "y = -(x - 3)² - 4",
      ],
      "title": "Final Check",
      "type": "quiz",
    },
    {
      "category": "Quadratics",
      "content": "You met quadratics from every angle: **standard form** (a, b, c), **vertex form** (h, k), **factored form** (the roots), the **discriminant**, and **factoring**. One curve, five lenses — that is what it means to *see* math instead of memorizing it.",
      "id": "you-did-it",
      "title": "You Did It!",
      "type": "text",
    },
  ],
}
`;

